Otto's Danish tool-budget message (`TOOL_BUDGET_MESSAGE_DA`) has to promise nothing concrete. It may not contain:
- a phone number, email address or opening hour;
- the words `ring`, `minutter` or `timer`;
- a persona name.

Spec FR-016 adds two more limits. The string must be non-empty, with no `<` character and no digit. A test checks that it uses only Danish letters, commas and full stops. It is also written in the first person and must not claim to be a person.

Issue #498 notes that the message currently ends with "En kollega vil følge op på din henvendelse." (a colleague will follow up). That issue is open and blocked, and it questions whether this promise is appropriate while no escalation destination exists.
